{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.IntraOrderingInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrderingInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.ChainTraceFactor","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BorromeanMarkovTrace","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.perGeneratorProduct_eq_grouped","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.perGeneratorProduct_eq_grouped","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L194-L199","doc":"The per-generator form is what the *grouped* assembly computes, by definition.\nStated so the contrast with `grouped_ne_borromean` is explicit: the identity\n`tr_M = ∏_gen tr₂` holds for the word whose generators are contiguous, and the\ninterleaved word does not satisfy it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.grouped_ne_borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.grouped_ne_borromean","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L189-L192","doc":"As functions of `q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.grouped_ne_borromean_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.grouped_ne_borromean_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L181-L187","doc":"**The grouped word is not `β_Bor`.** They already disagree at `q = 1`, where both\nare elementary — `1/4` against `1` — so the `82 %` gap measured at `q₀` is not a\ndeformation artefact but a difference of objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.groupedConfinement_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.groupedConfinement_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L174-L179","doc":"At `q = 1` the grouped per-generator product is `1/4`: each factor is\n`3/4 − 1/4 = 1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.wMinus_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.wMinus_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L171-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.wPlus_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.wPlus_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L168-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.borromeanConfinement_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.borromeanConfinement_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L162-L166","doc":"At the undeformed point `q = 1` the Borromean factor is `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.borromeanConfinement_le_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.borromeanConfinement_le_one","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L154-L160","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.borromeanConfinement_eq_one_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.borromeanConfinement_eq_one_sub","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L143-L152","doc":"The Borromean factor in the form that makes its size obvious:\n`1 − (3h⁴ + h⁶)/(h² + 4)`, so it is at most `1` and falls away from `1` at order `h⁴`.\n(At `q₀`, `h = 0.209…` and this is `0.998562…`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.trM_borromean_den_pos_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.trM_borromean_den_pos_real","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L140-L141","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.heckeH_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.heckeH_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L137-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.borromeanConfinement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.borromeanConfinement","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L132-L135","doc":"The **interleaved** confinement value: `|tr_M(β_Bor)|`, the closed form\n`(4 + h² − 3h⁴ − h⁶)/(h² + 4)` in `h = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.groupedConfinement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.groupedConfinement","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L128-L130","doc":"The **grouped** confinement value: the per-generator product, which is what a\nword with each generator's letters contiguous contributes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.twoStrandCubeInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.twoStrandCubeInv","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L124-L126","doc":"`tr₂(σ⁻³) = w₊ (q⁻¹)³ + w₋ (−q)³`, the mirror letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.twoStrandCube","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.twoStrandCube","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L121-L122","doc":"`tr₂(σ³) = w₊ q³ + w₋ (−q⁻¹)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.chainDiff_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.chainDiff_ne","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L103-L112","doc":"And it genuinely moves: the difference route distinguishes the orderings whenever\nthe intra factors differ and the interface product is not `1`. (At `q₀` every factor\n`z + d` lies in `(0,1)`, so `P ≠ 1` holds for every nonempty chain.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.chainDiff_scales","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.chainDiff_scales","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L96-L101","doc":"**`binding_canonical`'s `Δtr` is proportional to the intra factor.** Its\n`tr_M(W_free) − tr_M(W_atom)` equals `F (1 − P)`, so changing the ordering multiplies it\nby `F₁/F₂` — the same `3.785 … 14.325` the probe measures on the traces themselves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.L_chain_indep_of_intra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.L_chain_indep_of_intra","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L87-L92","doc":"Two orderings give the same `L`, for the same reason. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.L_chain_eq_sum_of_intra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.L_chain_eq_sum_of_intra","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L76-L85","doc":"**`L` is the interface sum whatever the intra ordering is.** For an arbitrary\nnonzero intra factor `F`, the bond constant read off the chain ratio is the sum of\n`-log(z + dᵢ)` over the interfaces. This is `ChainTraceFactor.neg_log_prod` transported\nthrough the cancellation above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.chainRatio_eq_of_intra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.chainRatio_eq_of_intra","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L68-L74","doc":"**Ordering invariance of the bond model.** Two intra orderings produce intra\nfactors `F₁` and `F₂`; no hypothesis relates them — in the measurement they differ by\nup to `14.325×` — and yet the chain ratio is the same. This is why `L`, the three bond\nconstants, and every log-ratio binding number are untouched by the ordering. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.chainRatio_eq_interfaceProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.IntraOrdering.chainRatio_eq_interfaceProd","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/IntraOrderingInvariance.lean#L63-L66","doc":"The chain ratio `tr_M(W_atom)/tr_M(W_free)` when the trace factors as\n`intra × interfaces`: the intra factor cancels. ","signatureChunk":0}]}